      "text": "Yes, you have a few options:\n\n1. **Fully Local (Current)** — Everything stays on-device using AsyncStorage. No login needed. Simple, private, works offline. Downside: data doesn't sync across devices and is lost if the app is uninstalled.\n\n2. **Optional Login** — App works locally by default, but users *can* sign in to sync/backup their summit data across devices. This is the best UX — no friction to start, with added value for signing in.\n\n3. **Required Login** — Users must sign in before using the app. Good if you want to build social features (leaderboards, sharing summit reports, following other climbers). Downside: adds friction and drops conversion.\n\n**My recommendation:** Go with **Option 2 (Optional Login)**. Let users start using the app immediately with local storage, and offer sign-in as a way to backup/sync data. This is what apps like Strava and AllTrails do — you can browse, but signing in unlocks more. \n\nWant me to implement one of these approaches?",
      "type": "text"
    }
